# axel — download accelerator

Axel accelerates downloads by requesting a file in small chunks over multiple HTTP/FTP connections at once.

## Basic accelerated download

```sh
axel https://download.opensuse.org/tumbleweed/iso/openSUSE-Tumbleweed-DVD-x86_64-Current.iso
```

## Real-world: more connections, custom output name

```sh
axel -n 8 -o ~/Downloads/tumbleweed.iso \
  https://download.opensuse.org/tumbleweed/iso/openSUSE-Tumbleweed-DVD-x86_64-Current.iso
```

## aria2 — multi-protocol alternative

aria2 is lightweight and supports HTTP(S), FTP, BitTorrent, and Metalink. It can pull one ISO from several mirrors simultaneously and works as a torrent client.

```sh
aria2c http://cdimage.debian.org/debian-cd/current/amd64/iso-cd/debian-netinst.iso
```

## Real-world: resume a huge interrupted download

```sh
# Both tools resume automatically if the partial file is present
axel -n 4 https://mirror.example.org/big-media-file.mkv
aria2c -c https://mirror.example.org/big-media-file.mkv
```

| Flag (axel) | What it does             |
| ----------- | ------------------------ |
| -n N        | number of connections    |
| -o FILE     | output filename          |
| -q          | quiet (for scripts)      |
